<%#
  What to do once the forms above are filled in.

  Two audiences, and the same facts. The steps are for reading; the prompt is
  for pasting into whatever the developer already has open. Neither is a
  template: both are assembled from what each module reports about THIS
  application right now, because a generic prompt produces plausible code
  against an API that does not exist.

  The prompt is a plain <textarea>, selected by a button when there is
  scripting and by dragging when there is not. Not a <pre> with a clipboard
  call and no fallback: this is the one control on the page whose entire
  purpose is getting text out, and it has to work without JavaScript.
%>
<h2 id="sparrowkit_implement" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-6 text-base font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Build on it</h2>
<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
  Installing is done &mdash; you could not be reading this page otherwise. This is
  how you call each module from your own code, generated from what is configured
  right now rather than from a manual.
</p>

<% @guided.each do |panel, guide| %>
  <% next if guide.steps.empty? %>
  <h3 class="mt-5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100"><%= panel.name %></h3>
  <ol class="mt-2 space-y-2">
    <% guide.steps.each do |step| %>
      <li>
        <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-slate-100 px-3 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200"><code><%= step %></code></pre>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ol>
<% end %>

<% if @prompt.present? %>
  <h3 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Or hand it to your assistant</h3>
  <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
    This describes what is installed, how it is configured, and the rules that
    matter &mdash; the ones a model would otherwise guess wrong, like billing the
    organization rather than the person. It contains no keys.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-3">
    <label for="sparrowkit_prompt" class="sr-only">Prompt describing this application's SparrowKit setup</label>
    <textarea id="sparrowkit_prompt"
              rows="12"
              readonly
              spellcheck="false"
              class="block w-full rounded-md border border-slate-500 bg-slate-100 px-3 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950 dark:text-slate-200"><%= @prompt %></textarea>
    <div class="mt-2 flex items-center gap-3">
      <button type="button"
              id="sparrowkit_prompt_copy"
              hidden
              class="rounded-md border border-slate-300 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 hover:border-purple-900 hover:text-purple-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:text-slate-200 dark:hover:border-purple-300 dark:hover:text-purple-300">
        Copy
      </button>
      <span id="sparrowkit_prompt_copied" role="status" class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-300"></span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%#
    Progressive enhancement, both ways round. The button starts hidden and is
    revealed by the script, so a browser with scripting off never shows a
    control that would do nothing -- the textarea is selectable regardless.
  %>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var button = document.getElementById("sparrowkit_prompt_copy");
      var field = document.getElementById("sparrowkit_prompt");
      var said = document.getElementById("sparrowkit_prompt_copied");
      if (!button || !field) return;

      button.hidden = false;
      button.addEventListener("click", function () {
        field.select();
        var done = function () { said.textContent = "Copied to your clipboard."; };
        // navigator.clipboard is unavailable on an insecure origin, which a
        // console served over plain http://localhost may or may not be
        // depending on the browser. execCommand still works there.
        if (navigator.clipboard && window.isSecureContext) {
          navigator.clipboard.writeText(field.value).then(done, function () {
            said.textContent = "Could not copy — the text is selected, so press Ctrl/Cmd+C.";
          });
        } else if (document.execCommand("copy")) {
          done();
        } else {
          said.textContent = "Could not copy — the text is selected, so press Ctrl/Cmd+C.";
        }
      });
    })();
  </script>
<% end %>
